.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt ELF_INIT_PPC32 3
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_init_ppc32
.Nd create a new ELF relocatable object configured for 32-bit PowerPC
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elfobj_t *
.Fn elf_init_ppc32 void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn elf_init_ppc32
function allocates a mutable
.Vt elfobj_t
and initializes it for 32-bit PowerPC relocatable output.
.Pp
The created object uses:
.Bl -tag -width "Architecture flags"
.It ELF type
.Dv ET_REL
.It Machine
.Dv EM_PPC
.It Class
.Dv ELFCLASS32
.It Data encoding
.Dv ELFDATA2MSB
.It Architecture flags
0
.El
.Pp
Default sections are created as part of initialization:
.Pa .text
(alignment 4),
.Pa .data
(alignment 4), and
.Pa .bss
(alignment 4).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn elf_init_ppc32
function returns a pointer to a newly allocated object on success.
On failure, it returns
.Dv NULL .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_finalize 3 ,
.Xr elf_close 3 ,
.Xr elfobj 3
